FriBidi bidi core, vendored for font-independent TEXT/MTEXT ordering.

Upstream: https://github.com/fribidi/fribidi
Release: 1.0.17
Archive: https://github.com/fribidi/fribidi/releases/download/v1.0.17/fribidi-1.0.17.tar.xz
SHA256: 6949dcde27d41cebad1fd741fcafc36d55a1020d2d872d4a6eb3914caabbada2
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later; see COPYING and the original file headers.
Unicode data: see COPYING.UNICODE.

Only the unchanged bidi algorithm, run allocator, bracket lookup and required
headers/tables are included. No Arabic shaping, charset conversion, tools or
generated bidi-type tables are needed. lc_textbidi.cpp supplies bidi properties
from QChar, so these match the application's Qt Unicode version. Bracket tables
are the release's Unicode 14 tables. Qt supplies grapheme boundaries and mirrors.

Both CMake and qmake compile the same three C sources as a private static
library. Build definitions select standard C allocation/string facilities,
disable upstream debug logging, and avoid a generated fribidi-config.h.

To update, verify the release archive, replace the corresponding files in src
without modifying their contents, preserve upstream notices, and rerun the bidi
and text rendering regressions (including headless tests). No system FriBidi
installation is required.
